{
 "name": "68-heading-unit-statement",
 "description": "A currency statement ('in', an optional scale word and 'of', and a currency name) on a line with no tab is a heading unit. It reaches the table rows as a heading scale does, and a unit item that holds it gives the field's unit there. A lone $ agrees with each dollar currency, so $m under 'presented in Australian dollars' gives AUD, and a USD field there goes to review. A unit form next to the value, or a field check that does not pass, makes the item fail (spec 0.10, #315). AUD has no form in the unit table, so it is at every token. Since spec 0.11, a unit item that holds its name repeats the unit and passes, as the candidate with no unit item passes (#423).",
